        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: William McKendree Gwin, John Charles Frémont\n- Roles: medical doctor, politician, explorer, businessman, presidential candidate\n- Places: Mississippi, California, United States\n- Organizations: Republican Party\n- Topics: elected office, anti-slavery politics\n\nFacts:\n- William McKendree Gwin was born on October 9, 1805, and died on September 3, 1885.\n- William McKendree Gwin was an American medical doctor and politician.\n- William McKendree Gwin served in elected office in Mississippi and California.\n- In California, William McKendree Gwin shared a distinction with John Charles Frémont.\n- John Charles Frémont was an American explorer, politician, and businessman.\n- In 1856, John Charles Frémont became the first presidential candidate of the anti-slavery Republican Party for President of the United States.",
